  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nThe current weather pattern over the Upper Ohio Valley and \nLower Great Lakes region is a general west-northwest flow aloft.\nThis pattern will continue to favor a mostly dry forecast with \noccasional wind shifts or weak cold fronts passing through which\nwill seesaw our temperatures at times later this week. High \npressure over the region is bringing fair skies this morning and\nsome cool temperatures, especially away from the lake. Today \nwill be sunny with high temperatures very close to our early \nOctober seasonal averages ranging from the lower 60s for NWPA, \nmiddle 60s for NEOH, and upper 60s for NWOH. It will not be as \ncool tonight with areas inland in the mid to upper 40s. High \npressure will exit eastward tomorrow and southwest winds will \nincrease 10 to 15 mph with gusts 20 to 25 mph during the \nafternoon. High temps on Wednesday will get an added boost and \nreach the lower to upper 70s across the area. \n\nA weak and dry cold front will move across late Wednesday night\ninto Thursday morning which will knock our temps back down \nslightly. Another area of high pressure and quiet weather will \nmove down across the Great Lakes and Ohio Valley for the end of \nthe week. High temperatures Thursday and Friday will range from \nthe mid 60s to low 70s. There will be a shift in our weather \npattern with slight upper level ridging developing over the \nregion by the weekend. Temperatures will warm back up Saturday \nand Sunday into the 70s areawide. There may be a couple \nlocations that try to reach the 80 degree over NWOH this \nweekend. The next chance of rain may arrive late Sunday into \nMonday with a remnant tropical system or low pressure system coming\nfrom the Gulf Coast region. It may brush by with some rainfall \nfor our area. There is alot of uncertainty at this time with the\nforecast that far out. In the meantime, enjoy the great weather\nthis week.",
